  <h3 class="sub" style="margin-top:0">Laboratory infrastructure</h3>
  <p><strong>Superorganism room:</strong> 28°C, 30% RH. Colonies housed in Fluon‑lined plastic trays (60×30×15cm). Artificial nests: foil‑wrapped petri dishes with moist plaster substrate. Fed 10% honey water + frozen insects (mealworms, crickets).</p>
  <p><strong>GC-MS (Shimadzu QP2020):</strong> DB-5 column, 60→300°C at 8°C/min. CHCs extracted with hexane + 0.1% docosane internal standard. SPME headspace sampling for volatiles.</p>
  <h3 class="sub">Microcolony assay design</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Positive control (+):</strong> 300 BB workers + 120 live Bb workers (mesh barrier for 48h, then full contact before queen introduction).</li>
    <li><strong>Negative control (−):</strong> 300 BB workers only.</li>
    <li><strong>Open‑lid treatment:</strong> Full physical contact allowed for 24h before adding two polygyne queens.</li>
    <li><strong>Venom sac extraction:</strong> Bb workers chilled, dissected under stereomicroscope, venom glands stored at -20°C. Extract will be applied to BB workers to test behavioral induction.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="sticky" style="margin-top:9px">🧪 28 positive/negative control replicates completed. Venom sac dissection ongoing.</div>
</div>
